{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07AF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : T \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/T)_\\tau$", "MATH_0004": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$R^if_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-direct-image-parasitic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1d0d69f9766b2e3d4a76f33cd7b9db8e04d21594cb589df73290d1b9954f329", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f2edf548b099695e543976eddba8aaa93051484954bc50241e7031056a33f6d4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. For any parasitic\n<MATH_0002>-module on <MATH_0003> the pushforward\n<MATH_0004> and the higher direct images <MATH_0005>\nare parasitic <MATH_0006>-modules on <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5fac4827c990cc54d1a1e3ae29807481d41cdf93c46ad2753149ca6e6afedc5c", "unit_id": "tag:07AG:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07AF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R^if_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nU \\mapsto H^i((\\Sch/U \\times_S T)_\\tau, \\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\times_S T \\to T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0007": "$U_i \\times_S T \\to T$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-higher-direct-images}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-cohomology-parasitic}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f4ec2cf92c7a4c4fab97cb210265c5cce1504cface4a2795ea8cf1a4f7a6526c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2f8cf0c9aa36198047837973e3dfa941ad55343e4d5503485123f836728ef8e", "source_text": "Recall that <MATH_0001> is the sheaf associated to the\npresheaf\n<MATH_0002>\nsee\nCohomology on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is flat, then <MATH_0004> is flat as a base change.\nHence the displayed group is zero by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0005> is a <MATH_0006>-covering then\n<MATH_0007> is also flat.\nHence it is clear that the sheafification of the displayed\npresheaf is zero on schemes <MATH_0008> flat over <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:40883886b629d5b3c4f1558b9811140eb8c6bd69f4849de0410540d18fa2799e", "unit_id": "tag:07AG:proof"}
